hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15951","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said, Khalid narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I sat with a group, I being their fourth, at Iliya. One of them said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall enter Paradise through the intercession of a man of my umma more than Banu Tamim. We said: Other than you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Other than me. I said: Did you hear it yourself? He said: Yes. When he stood, I said: Who is this? They said: Ibn Abi al-Jad'a."
